## 6. Windows Logon Types

Logon Types are commonly found in Security Event IDs `4624` and `4625`.

| Logon Type | Description |
|---|---|
| **2** | Interactive — local sign-in |
| **3** | Network — access over a network |
| **4** | Batch — scheduled or batch job |
| **5** | Service — service logon |
| **7** | Unlock — workstation unlocked |
| **8** | NetworkCleartext |
| **9** | NewCredentials |
| **10** | RemoteInteractive — Remote Desktop |
| **11** | CachedInteractive — cached domain credentials |

> **SOC Tip:** A logon type provides context, not proof of malicious activity. For example, Type 3 and Type 10 logons can both occur during legitimate operations.

