## 10. PowerShell Commands for Event Log Analysis

PowerShell provides another way to search and analyze Windows event logs.

Run PowerShell as Administrator if access to the Security log requires elevated permissions.

### List Available Event Logs

```powershell
Get-WinEvent -ListLog *
```

### Display the Latest Security Events

```powershell
Get-WinEvent -LogName Security -MaxEvents 20
```

### Find Failed Logons

```powershell
Get-WinEvent -FilterHashtable @{
    LogName = 'Security'
    Id = 4625
} -MaxEvents 50
```

### Find Successful Logons

```powershell
Get-WinEvent -FilterHashtable @{
    LogName = 'Security'
    Id = 4624
} -MaxEvents 50
```

